{
  "about": "The W over P rows of the MCU speed matrix (docs/mcu-speed-matrix.md, decision D10 of docs/upstream-parity.md carried to an emulated MCU), judged by `scripts/host-bench/mcu_speed.py --gate` after every run of `scripts/mcu-speed.sh`. A row is the cost ratio of one held figure of one cell, keyed <machine>/<threads>/<workload>/<size>/<figure> (wz's over zenoh-pico's for a figure better lower, the reverse for one better higher; below 1 is wz ahead): {\"locked\": true} holds the cell to WIN, {\"ratio_at_most\": R} holds the upper end of its bootstrap interval to R times one plus `tolerance`, {\"reference_lost\": WHY} records a cell the reference lost every repetition of, and null is not filled yet, a failure whose sentence prints the row a run writes. The rows are the population of the default matrix on `platform` (`--check-table`); a row is written only from the gate's own output for a run, never by hand. `platform` is the board, the QEMU machine and core and the -icount shift the rows are read on; the gate refuses a run on another platform against them.",
